  "question": {
    "text": "The organic chloro compound, which shows complete stereochemical inversion during a $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2$ reaction, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xU1RL",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{H}_5\\right)_2 \\mathrm{CHCl}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "G11lL",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3 \\mathrm{CCl}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nbeAI",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_2 \\mathrm{CHCl}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Od1MS",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{Cl}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2$ reaction, the $\\mathrm{C}$ atom is least hindered towards the attack of nucleophile in the case of $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{Cl}\\right)$.\nHence, (D) is the correct answer.",
    "image": null
  },
